"""Explainer pillar - Roof Load Limits by Vehicle.
No invented testing. Every figure in the chart comes from the site's stored vehicle data (db/migrations/003_vehicles.sql:
roof_type, roof_load_lb and the attrs research notes), from the site's roof rack and cargo box guides and the maker, dealer,
retailer and forum pages those guides cite, or from pages opened on 2026-10-08 (Tesla Model Y owner's manual, Vehicle
Loading page: no roof load printed; Ford support pages on roof rack limits: no figure in the page text; the 2023 Grand
Cherokee owner's manual PDF, whose Roof Luggage Rack section could not be read). Where the site stores no figure, the row
says "not published / not confirmed" and names what was found instead. The site's roof_load_lb for the RAV4 (165 lb) and
the 2010-2024 4Runner (120 lb) are carried as the site's own unconfirmed working figures, as the guides describe them.
"""

KIND = "explainer"
SLUG = "roof-load-limits-by-vehicle"
CATEGORIES = ["roof-racks", "cargo-boxes"]

TITLE = "Roof Load Limits by Vehicle: Rack and Cargo Box Weight Limits for 32 Trucks and SUVs"
